WEBVTT

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.530
I'll be late...

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.420
Wash my face...

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.880
Brush my teeth...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.960
Where's my toothbrush?

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.050
Mom...

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.890
Where's my toothbrush?

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.000
Ow...

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.450
What's her problem?

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:09.910
<i>That's right...</i>

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:14.910
<i>All that weird stuff happened to me!</i>

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:52.730
<i>I got sent to this strange place, 
and it was awful,</i>

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:55.280
<i>so I freaked out.</i>

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.450
That was great!

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.030
That food was good...

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.100
Anyway...

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:15.670
Still no reception?

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:21.180
Oda Nobunaga.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.080
A Warring States period general.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:26.840
Lived from 1534 to 1582...

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:28.850
Akechi Mitsuhide.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:33.170
<i>I am Oda Nobunaga.</i>

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.340
<i>My name is Akechi Mitsuhide.</i>

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:44.200
<b>History</b>

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:40.200
But they're girls, not guys.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:44.200
Think maybe they really 
are historical cosplayers?

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:50.750
And this building definitely isn't normal.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.400
This is all really weird.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.750
I don't get it...

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:02.590
But right now, my biggest problem

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:06.600
is that all I have are my 
school uniform and gym clothes!

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.620
I look lame...

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:08.840
This is awful.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:09.850
I'm coming in.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:20.480
You wear the strangest outfits.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:26.370
<b>Episode 2</b>

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:26.370
<b>A Confused Maiden</b>

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.700
Pick whichever you like from these.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:33.770
What is this? A mountain of treasure!

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:35.470
There are so many!

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:37.090
So amazing!

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:39.420
Can I really, truly pick the ones I like?

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.210
Yeah...

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.090
This is so cute!

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.100
What do you think?

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.590
Don't ask me.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.840
I suppose it's fine.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:53.430
Maybe I'll make some alterations to it.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.740
Lend me a sewing kit later, OK?

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:57.990
Excuse me.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:01.730
My lord, all is in readiness—

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:03.760
Yeah?

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:05.530
You come, too.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:09.030
Where?

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:13.910
U-Um, is this really OK?

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.510
There aren't seat belts or anything.

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.180
I'm not gonna fall, am I?

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:18.500
Hang on tight!

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:21.660
My butt!

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:22.900
My butt!

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:25.130
My butt...

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.980
Looks like it isn't going well.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:41.860
No.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:45.200
Ow...

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.240
We were here last night!

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.290
There, there...

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:56.210
There's barely anything left.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.280
Be careful, all right?

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:02.420
It looks like there are enough people here.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.460
All have lost their homes...

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.020
falling into despair.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:12.100
Everyone, listen!

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.940
Our lord has come here personally.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:18.230
Be thankful for her kindness,

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:24.810
and work harder, despite your sorrow!

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.320
You can't do that.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:31.950
I don't think that will work.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.620
What?

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:37.480
I don't think you can just say something,

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:39.960
and expect it to cheer them up 
or fill their bellies.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:45.750
We should at least give them 
some delicious candy or a cheerful song!

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.590
What are you saying?

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:50.380
So then, what would you do?

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:53.560
Me?

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.980
Here you go... Here you go.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:04.810
Pretty, isn't it?

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:08.990
Here!

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.160
Ta-dah!

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.200
That contraption again?

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:28.760
Start the music!

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:28.760
<b>Dreaming Freedom</b>

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.760
We want stuff we can still use, right?

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:39.640
Let's get started!

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.890
What can we use...

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.040
Everyone!

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.480
I think we can still use this pot.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:52.950
Hurry! Hurry!

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.700
It's heavy... Hurry!

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.620
Is it still useful?

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:03.940
Good...

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.840
This will still work, too.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:16.100
Look at your face!

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.580
There!

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:45.450
Can you get us some 
food and sweets, Mitsuhide-san?

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.830
Very well.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:49.000
Fetch some from the storehouse.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.960
But, my lord, that's...

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.880
Mitsuhide.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.130
Retrieve some.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:56.840
This is the last time, right?

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:26.580
She's done well.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:31.310
She easily captured the peasants' hearts.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:38.300
She will be a fresh wind, 
as we cannot foresee.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.600
You think so?

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:42.600
I am not mistaken about such things.

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:49.400
Miss... Here's a meat bun for you!

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.010
A meat bun?

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:52.550
They look good...

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:54.580
Thank you!

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:57.570
<i>Huh?</i>

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:00.490
<i>Come to think of it, 
why are only women here?</i>

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:08.670
Um...

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:10.610
Here?

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.600
I can make this my room?

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:17.420
Our lord grants you this, 
as a reward for your efforts today.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:19.900
What's wrong?

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:20.850
You're dissatisfied?

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:23.140
This room is more than good enough for you.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.930
No, no! That's not it at all.

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:28.830
It's just that the interior 
design isn't quite right.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:31.210
May I coordinate it a little?

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:32.940
The interior cord?

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.280
Coordinate, you know...

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.080
Uh, are you not good with foreign words?

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:39.320
How rude!

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.300
Don't get mad...

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:45.380
But yeah, I have a request...

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:51.820
It was totally worth asking.

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:55.940
Anyway, that Mitsuhide person 
gets mad really easily.

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:57.550
Just like Akerin.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.850
It's hard to believe that I'm only 
meeting her for the first time.

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:00.930
Her personality...

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:04.190
Ow...

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:04.970
Keh.

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:09.640
Keh.

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:11.310
You!

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:14.320
<i>Who the hell are you?</i>

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.170
<i>Did you wander in somehow?</i>

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.160
<i>Wait!</i>

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:24.580
You're from yesterday...

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:27.950
That weird dog.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:42.850
So, how come you can talk?

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:46.510
The same reason that 
you're here, I suppose.

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:48.950
The world contains many mysterious things.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:50.930
That doesn't make any sense.

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:53.000
I'd like to ask you something.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:54.570
I have a name, you know.

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:57.610
My name is Shiro, girl.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:58.980
So, your name's Shiro?

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:00.490
Don't use it so carelessly!

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.260
Then what should I call you?

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:06.200
I'll grant you special permission 
to call me Shiro-sama.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.830
"Sama"? You're a dog.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:10.960
I can hear you, damn it.

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:14.940
Hey... Where am I?

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:18.070
A different world than 
the one you inhabited,

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.460
one far in the past.

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:22.210
In the past... And a different...

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:24.220
A different world?

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:25.440
No way!

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:28.760
That only happens in light novels and manga.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:32.470
And are there any men here?

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:34.270
I haven't seen any...

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:36.770
About that...

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:41.780
Well, you see... 
There aren't any, well, men here...

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:48.200
Then how is everyone born?

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.620
Because babies are...

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:55.040
Right?

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:58.490
I dare you to repeat that.

00:12:58.490 --> 00:13:00.370
Never mind...

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:02.550
Anyway, tell me the reason.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.050
You see...

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:07.050
You see...

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:14.100
The stork brings them...

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.150
Was that really worth the dramatic pause?

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.110
And why is your personality changing?

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:24.700
And they're found in cabbage fields...

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:29.460
Or sometimes, in a bamboo stalk...

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:30.640
I see!

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:33.900
In old stories, that's how it always is.

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:37.070
And this is a different world, 
in the past, so that makes sense!

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:41.890
Then, how do I get back?

00:13:41.890 --> 00:13:43.790
Um, well...

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:46.140
I doubt it'll be easy.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:51.620
But not 100% certain 
that I can't return, right?

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:52.930
I suppose...

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:56.660
OK!

00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:58.990
In these situations, the main character

00:13:58.990 --> 00:14:00.830
must always do her best!

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:03.650
And sometimes, that hard work 
takes her home!

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:07.940
You really are easygoing.

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:08.660
Just stupid?

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:12.490
You know what they say... 
When in Rome, do as the Swiss do, right?

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.940
No one says that anymore, 
and it's wrong anyway.

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:17.820
Hey, help me decorate, Shiro.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:20.660
If I'm going to be here a while, 
I want to make it cute.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:21.410
Right?

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:23.150
I'd even take a dog's help.

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:25.720
The saying's about a cat, not a dog.

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:28.480
You don't know anything, do you?

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:29.890
You're a moron.

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:44.920
Wake up, already!

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:47.640
Let me rest a bit more...

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:48.400
Get up!

00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:52.360
Hey!

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:54.070
You're too loud!

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:55.240
Who's loud?

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:56.500
Who...

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:10.460
Shiro kept telling me to wake up...

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:11.530
Shiro?

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:16.990
Why is he acting like that?

00:15:16.990 --> 00:15:18.650
What's wrong with you?

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:20.260
And what is this?

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:23.590
How dare you do this to 
the room the lord gave you?

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:24.820
It's cute, isn't it?

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:27.910
Where do you think you are?

00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:28.860
You're being loud...

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.750
My lord, look at this!

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:34.820
Oh, my...

00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:36.240
I like this.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:39.200
You, also, my lord? What are you...

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:41.620
Isn't it nice?

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.030
Right, huh?

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.790
You arrogant little...

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:49.550
I'll show you what it means to be a warrior!

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.680
<b>Six-Round Match 
6  5  4  3  2  1</b>

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:08.190
I shall show this girl how to be a warrior.

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:13.070
I look forward to seeing your skills.

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:16.370
Um...

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:18.910
Now! Let the battle begin!

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.550
Here I go!

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:36.850
Your turn.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:45.450
Huh?

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:52.570
Ow...

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:54.700
I'm a demon!

00:16:57.610 --> 00:16:58.690
Huh?

00:16:58.690 --> 00:16:59.950
I slipped?

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:28.480
Uncle! Uncle! Uncle!

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:42.910
You can't do anything, can you?

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:45.910
Give me a break...

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:53.130
This is the final one!

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:57.130
Here I go!

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:01.010
This isn't working.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:06.100
You're embarrassing yourself!

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.480
I don't want to do this anymore!

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:17.940
That surprised me!

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:20.260
But I've seen that before...

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.400
What are you doing, 
turning away from an enemy?

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:23.620
How pathetic!

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.120
That's it! That's the one...

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.350
That Tokunyan, Akerin, and I always 
chatted about on our phones!

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:28.540
What was it?

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:30.380
Kung Fat!

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:31.380
Right!

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:33.380
I remember!

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:40.010
Um, I think it was like...

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:42.220
Kung Fat is here!

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:50.480
What is that skill?

00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:52.910
It's kung fu.

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:54.230
Don't you know it?

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:56.860
More nonsense!

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:58.370
In situations like these,

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:02.160
the hero always makes a 
big comeback and wins, right?

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:05.870
Come on! Come on!

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:08.040
How dare you?

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:25.430
Huh?

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:31.850
Mitsuhide won every match,

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:35.320
but that final battle was quite entertaining.

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:39.570
What? Kung Fat won with that.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:40.430
This can't be!

00:19:40.430 --> 00:19:43.170
Where did you learn that skill?

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:44.550
Where?

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:45.200
On TV!

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.830
You've never heard of Kung Fat?

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:51.560
He's a fat guy who uses kung fu...

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:53.350
You wouldn't have, would you?

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:54.840
Whatever.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:58.820
You moved just like a monkey. 
It was splendid.

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:00.130
I know.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:02.590
From now on, I'll call you Monkey.

00:20:03.950 --> 00:20:05.930
I don't want that nickname!

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.410
Then call me Hideyoshi!

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:10.080
Everyone does.

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.700
That's no fun.

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:13.620
Then, Hideyoshi...

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:16.980
Continue to practice 
martial arts with Mitsuhide.

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:19.520
Martial arts, huh?

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:20.930
Well, why not?

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:22.590
Thanks, Mitsuhide-san...

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:25.630
I think I'll call you Akerin.

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:26.950
It feels more right.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:28.540
A-Akerin?

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:29.850
What is that?

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:31.500
You can't call me that!

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.920
Oh, come on... Let's be friends!

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:35.750
Oh, are you a tsundere?

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:36.850
Huh?

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:38.200
Hideyoshi.

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:40.560
From now on, you are my retainer.

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:42.300
Call me "my lord."

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:44.720
My lord?

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:47.810
Um... What does that mean?

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:53.770
You are a strange person, 
you know that?

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:00.680
So it means I'm an official retainer

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:03.450
for this Nobunaga person now?

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.870
That's right.

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:09.520
I see...

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:12.320
Girl.

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:14.940
It's an honor wasted on you.

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:16.480
Show more cheer.

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:18.180
It is?

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:20.340
OK, I'll be cheerful!

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:21.320
Yay!

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:22.130
Whoo!

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:24.170
She's a real idiot.

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:27.640
But an interesting girl.

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:31.500
I took the ancient scroll 
you gave me, Masamune,

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:32.980
and investigated personally.

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:35.580
And I've learned that Imagawa Yoshimoto

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:38.630
has the armor's left leg.

00:21:40.270 --> 00:21:41.480
Then you leave immediately?

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:45.990
Yes. My lord and I leave for negotiations.

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:47.610
Who's that?

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:48.990
That?

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:53.040
My lord brought in that girl, 
Hideyoshi, a while ago.

00:21:54.280 --> 00:22:00.100
What was she thinking, 
bringing in someone we know nothing of?

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:01.670
Hideyoshi...

00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:04.490
Fetch!

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:07.120
I don't like behaving like a dog.

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:10.010
But you are a dog!

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:42.260
Remember what we learned

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:42.940
<b>Date-Sensei 
Hirata Yuka</b>

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:52.490
<b>Sengoku Otome Style Preview</b>

00:23:42.260 --> 00:23:43.610
about the Battle of Okehazama?

00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:45.200
Both were <i>hazama</i>  — between — the buckets, <i>oke</i>,

00:23:43.980 --> 00:23:46.280
<b>Hideyoshino 
Hidaka Rina</b>

00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:46.570
trying to take the other's bucket.

00:23:46.570 --> 00:23:50.000
So, who was trying to grab the buckets?

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:51.610
Imagawa Yoshimoto and...

00:23:51.610 --> 00:23:52.490
Yup, that's right.

00:23:52.510 --> 00:23:54.560
Preview

00:23:52.510 --> 00:23:54.560
Sky Maiden

00:23:52.900 --> 00:23:54.650
Watch next time, OK?
